ITEM_ROLES = [('damage','Offense'),('shieldmagic','Defense'),('position','Mobility'),('clock','Action economy'),('utility','Utility'),('coins','Value')]
# name: (ratings, grade, band, evaluation)
I = {}
def i(n, r, g, band, ev): I[n] = (r, g, band, ev)

# ── Permanent: attachments ──
i('Clay Sphere','300024','A','Levels 3–8',"Clay Sphere is the weapon spellheart that best suits Cyrus. Its basic version casts Gouging Claw, which frees one of his five cantrip slots for a utility cantrip. The greater version casts Enlarge once a day, and after a morph or polymorph cast it makes Aspera versatile in bludgeoning, piercing and slashing and steps up its damage die until the end of his next turn. With one or two fights a day, that daily boost is available in most fights. It occupies Aspera's single talisman or spellheart slot.")
i('Flaming Star','300003','B','Levels 3–8',"Flaming Star casts Ignition and adds 1d4 fire damage to Strikes until the end of Cyrus's next turn after he casts a fire spell through it. It is a good alternative to Clay Sphere for campaign arcs heavy in trolls, undead or other creatures weak to fire.")
i('Jolt Coil','300003','B','Levels 3–12',"Jolt Coil casts Electric Arc, and its greater version casts Lightning Bolt once a day at a fixed DC. It adds 1d4 electricity to Strikes after an electricity cast. It pairs naturally with Cyrus's electricity payloads, but the fixed DC of its daily spell will fall behind his own.")
i('Phantasmal Doorknob','200013','B','Levels 6–10',"Phantasmal Doorknob makes weapon critical hits leave the target dazzled until the end of its next turn. Dazzled is a modest debuff: the target treats everything as concealed, so its own attacks and targeted spells face a DC 5 flat check, but it is not blinded. Its daily spell is cast at the item's fixed DC, which falls behind Cyrus's own DC at higher levels. It is a reasonable mid-level attachment rather than an essential one.")
i('Sunweave','000132','B','Levels 7+',"Sunweave is an armour property rune that grants +1 to Perception and a once-a-day initiative reroll. With one or two fights a day, the reroll is available in most fights, which helps Cyrus act before the enemy and set up the party.")

# ── Permanent: worn ──
i('Ancestral Geometry','050015','A','Levels 2–4',"Ancestral Geometry lets Cyrus roll 2d20 each morning, keep the higher result, and use it as a reaction to replace one saving throw of a randomly chosen type. It also gives a Lore bonus that Alex chooses. At 30 gp it is the cheapest worthwhile invested item, and with one or two fights a day the stored roll is available in most fights.")
i("Healer's Gloves",'000044','A','Levels 4–9',"Healer's Gloves restore 2d6+7 Hit Points to an adjacent ally once a day for one action, or 4d6+15 for the greater version, and give a bonus to Medicine. With one or two fights a day, that is an emergency heal in most fights that doesn't use the Cleric's actions. It is one of the best early purchases for keeping the party standing.")
i('Lifting Belt','200013','B','Levels 4–8',"Lifting Belt gives +1 to Athletics and raises Cyrus's carrying capacity. The Athletics bonus improves every Trip, Grapple and Reposition. It should be replaced by Armbands of Athleticism at level 9.")
i('Armbands of Athleticism','300023','A','Levels 9+',"Armbands of Athleticism give +2 to Athletics and extra distance on successful Climb and Swim checks. Trip, Grapple, Shove and Reposition all use Athletics, so the armbands improve every setup turn Cyrus takes. They are a priority from level 9.")
i("Tactician's Helm",'000343','B','Levels 5–10',"Tactician's Helm gives +1 to Warfare Lore and gains a charge each time Cyrus hits with Reactive Strike. A charge powers a one-action double Stride, a bonus to Athletics and Acrobatics, or three Interacts. The Interact option lets him drink a potion and regrip Aspera cheaply. It depends on Reactive Strike hits to charge, so it only becomes useful from level 6.")
i('Boots of Bounding','000403','B','Levels 7–12',"Boots of Bounding give a +5-foot item bonus to Speed and improve jumps. Item bonuses stack with Laughing Shadow's status bonus, and Dimensional Assault's range is based on Speed, so the boots extend his teleports as well as his movement.")
i('Propulsive Boots','000542','A','Levels 13+',"Propulsive Boots give +5 feet of Speed and, once a day, one action of quickened for a minute that can be used to Stride, Climb or Swim. With one or two fights a day, that is an extra move action every turn of the main fight. They replace Boots of Bounding.")
i('Retrieval Belt','000403','B','Levels 7+',"Retrieval Belt stores one item, or more in higher versions, and retrieves it into a free hand as a free action, with a one-minute cooldown. Keeping a healing potion or a key scroll in it removes the draw action while Aspera is in hand.")
i('Master Magus Ring','000552','A','Levels 11+',"Master Magus Ring grants +2 to Arcana, a free Focus Point once a day for a conflux spell, and a free teleport up to Cyrus's Speed once a day. With one or two fights a day, that is an extra Dimensional Assault and a free escape in most fights. It is one of the strongest items for his build.")
i('Kindler Cameo','140022','C','Not on general sale',"Kindler Cameo is an invested once-a-day heal of 3d10+12 Hit Points with a status bonus to Will saves and an instant end to persistent damage. That is a solid emergency button at level 7, but it costs two actions and needs a free hand, which means letting go of Aspera and regripping, so in practice it is a three-action turn. Its other ability is tied to one adventure location and does nothing here. It is worth an invested slot only if Cyrus has nothing better, which by level 7 is rarely true.")

# ── Permanent: spell access ──
i('Endless Grimoire','000023','B','Levels 6+',"Endless Grimoire lets Cyrus prepare an extra spell each day, at rank 1 for the base version and rising to rank 3, 5 and 7 for the greater, major and true versions. It also improves Learn a Spell checks. The base version gives one more Sure Strike or utility spell, which is modest; the higher versions are more valuable.")
i('Ring of Wizardry','000023','B','Levels 7+',"Ring of Wizardry is a legacy item, still available here, that grants two extra rank-1 arcane slots for 360 gp, with higher types granting higher slots. Cyrus already has two rank-1 slots for one or two fights a day, so the extra slots mainly go to utility spells.")
i('Spellstriker Staff','300033','A','Levels 7–11',"Spellstriker Staff contains Sure Strike, Acid Grip and Telekinetic Maneuver, all excellent for Cyrus, and triggers an explosion when a Spellstrike misses. It is the best published stopgap if Aspera's bespoke stave is delayed, and Fused Staff at 8 lets him use it without letting go of Aspera.")
i('Staff of the Unblinking Eye','000033','B','Levels 6–10',"Staff of the Unblinking Eye contains Sure Strike, See the Unseen and other detection spells, and gives +1 to initiative while held. It is weaker than the Spellstriker Staff for Cyrus but a reasonable alternative for scouting.")

# ── Consumables ──
i('Healing Potion','040033','A','Always',"A healing potion restores Hit Points immediately, which is what matters when Cyrus is about to fall. He should always carry one of an appropriate level, ideally loaded in a Potion Patch so he can drink it without releasing Aspera.")
i("Cat's Eye Elixir",'300024','A','Levels 2+',"Cat's Eye Elixir removes the flat check against concealed targets and lowers it to 5 against hidden ones within 30 feet for a minute. That protects a decisive Spellstrike against blurred, invisible or fog-shrouded enemies without spending Sure Strike.")
i('Mistform Elixir','040003','B','Levels 4+',"Mistform Elixir makes Cyrus concealed for its duration. Against archers or a single heavy hitter, it causes a fifth of their attacks to miss outright. It is best drunk just before a known dangerous fight.")
i('Numbing Tonic','040003','B','Levels 1+',"Numbing Tonic grants temporary Hit Points immediately and again at the start of each of Cyrus's turns for a minute. Drunk before a boss fight, it absorbs a meaningful amount of damage over the encounter.")
i('Soothing Tonic','030003','C','Levels 2+',"Soothing Tonic grants fast healing for a minute. It restores Hit Points steadily but too slowly to save Cyrus from immediate danger, so a healing potion is usually the better choice.")
i('Potion of Quickness','000502','B','Levels 8+',"Potion of Quickness grants the effects of Haste for a minute. It is a strong backup for a decisive fight when no one has Haste prepared, and loaded in a Potion Patch it takes one action without releasing Aspera.")
i('Transmuting Ingot','300014','A','Levels 1+',"A Transmuting Ingot makes Aspera count as silver, cold iron or adamantine for a minute. Carrying one silver and one cold-iron ingot lets Cyrus exploit the weaknesses of devils, demons, fey and lycanthropes for a few gold pieces.")
i('Analysis Eye','000013','C','Levels 4+',"Analysis Eye reveals one weakness or resistance on the first successful Strike against each creature. Magus's Analysis already gives Cyrus a Recall Knowledge check every turn, so this adds little.")
i('Potency Crystal','300003','C','Levels 1+',"Potency Crystal gives temporary fundamental runes for one Strike. Aspera has its runes, so it only helps a backup weapon.")
i('Ghostbane Fulu','300003','B','Levels 6+',"Ghostbane Fulu gives Aspera ghost touch against one incorporeal creature for a minute. It is a cheap answer to a known haunting before Ghostly Weapon becomes a studious spell at level 11.")
i('Escape Fulu','040203','C','Levels 7+',"Escape Fulu gives +2 to Escape and to Stealth to Hide and Sneak for a minute. It is worth carrying against known grapplers.")
i('Emerald Grasshopper','000403','B','Levels 5+',"Emerald Grasshopper lets Cyrus Leap up to 40 feet for one action without letting go of Aspera, and falls gently if he ends in the air. It solves gaps, ledges and rooftop routes.")
i('Blast Boots','000303','C','Levels 1+',"Blast Boots let Cyrus High Jump or Long Jump without a running start, with greater distance at higher levels. Activating them requires a free hand, which costs Aspera's grip.")
i('Gecko Pads','000203','C','Levels 5+',"Gecko Pads give a climb Speed while Cyrus's hands are free. Gecko Grip becomes a studious spell at 7 and does the same without freeing his hands.")
i('Retrieval Prism','000403','B','Levels 3+',"Retrieval Prism is a talisman that teleports one attuned item into a free hand as a free action, once. Paired with a healing potion, it saves the draw action in an emergency.")
i('Potion Patch','000503','A','Levels 4+',"Potion Patch lets Cyrus drink a loaded potion for one action without needing a hand free. For a character who holds a two-handed weapon, it is the most efficient way to make potions usable in combat.")
i('Oil of Skating','000302','C','Levels 2+',"Oil of Skating gives +10 feet of status Speed on flat ground for an hour. It overlaps Laughing Shadow's status bonus, so the benefit is small.")
i('Oil of Potency','300002','C','Levels 2+',"Oil of Potency gives temporary fundamental runes for a minute. It only helps a backup weapon.")
i('Energizing Tea','200103','C','Levels 4+',"Energizing Tea gives +1 to Athletics and Acrobatics for 10 minutes, or an hour after a tea ceremony. Armbands of Athleticism make it redundant from level 9.")
i('Heartening Missive (Butterfly)','000013','C','Levels 5+',"Heartening Missive (Butterfly) lets its recipient improve one failed Diplomacy or Performance check by a degree once in the next 24 hours. It is a social tool to send before an important negotiation.")
i('Explosive Missive','300002','C','Levels 4+',"Explosive Missive deals 4d6 damage in a small burst at a fixed DC. Cyrus's own spells deal more damage at a better DC.")
i('Bottled Lightning','200102','C','Levels 1+',"Bottled Lightning is a thrown bomb that leaves the target off-guard. It works better in the hands of a ranged ally who can set up Cyrus's Laughing Shadow damage.")
i('Smoke Ball','030203','C','Levels 1+',"Smoke Ball creates a burst of concealing smoke. It covers a retreat but hampers the party's own targeting.")

# ── Runes for Aspera ──
i('Fearsome','300013','B','Level 5',"Fearsome makes critical hits leave the target frightened 1, or frightened 2 for the greater version. Frightened lowers the target's AC and saves for the whole party, and the rune is cheap.")
i('Astral','300013','B','Level 8',"Astral grants ghost touch and an extra 1d6 spirit damage. It is a strong choice if undead and spirits recur in the campaign.")
i('Rooting','230002','B','Level 7',"Rooting makes critical hits immobilise the target and leave it clumsy while immobilised. Clumsy lowers its Reflex DC, which helps Cyrus's Trip.")
i('Frost','320002','A','Level 8',"Frost adds 1d6 cold damage and can slow the target on a critical hit. Slowed is one of the strongest conditions in the game, which makes this the best general-purpose property rune for Aspera.")
i('Shock','300002','A','Level 8',"Shock adds 1d6 electricity damage, and critical hits arc to two more enemies. It is a strong damage rune for a weapon that crits often.")
i('Ghost Touch','200003','C','Level 4',"Ghost Touch lets Aspera fully affect incorporeal creatures. Ghostly Weapon and the Astral rune cover this more efficiently.")
i('Wounding','300003','B','Level 7',"Wounding adds 1d6 persistent bleed on every hit. Persistent damage of the same type doesn't stack, so it overlaps with Gouging Claw's bleed rather than adding to it.")
i('Shifting','000303','C','Level 6',"Shifting lets Aspera change into another two-handed weapon. A signature weapon rarely needs this.")
i('Grievous','220002','C','Level 9',"Grievous improves critical specialisation effects. The magus doesn't gain critical specialisation on its own, so Cyrus would see little benefit.")
